"""Factual domain/selection plan for already-read Schema and SDK source bytes.
This creates review projections only; it never imports or executes product code.
"""
DOMAINS = [
 ("schema.session-instruction", "Agent, behavior, skill and prompt instruction contracts", "Identify host/agent-owned instructions and distinguish configuration from permission and provider execution.", "Agent files declare optimistic revisions and ordered permission rules; agent DTOs carry engine/model/toolkit and permissions. Prompt context is host-owned rendered reminders. Skills define catalog/source/save identities; subagent policy constrains delegated model identities.", "Applying configuration, resolving files, enforcing permissions and executing turns belong to host/Core services. No execution or persistence guarantee follows from these DTOs."),
 ("schema.permission-question", "Permission decisions and questions", "Identify session-linked request/reply shapes, saved permissions and historical rule compatibility before interpreting approval endpoints.", "Permission replies are once/always/reject; modern rules use action/resource/effect while stored Session overrides retain permission/pattern/action. Questions bind session IDs and ordered answers. A request ID or pair of parameters alone is not an ownership check.", "Core request lookup, approval authorization, persistence and race behavior remain required before asserting effective session ownership or decision application."),
 ("schema.session-projections", "Session activity, revert, todo and compaction projections", "Distinguish representable session facts and invalidations from the calculations/mutations producing them.", "Revert carries message/part and optional snapshot/diff/files; activity represents counts/times and a truncated flag; compaction/todo events carry session identity. Todo status and priority are strings with descriptions, not closed enums.", "Activity computation, revert effects, compaction execution and todo storage are delegated service facts, not established by these wire shapes."),
 ("schema.project-identity", "Identifiers, projects, workspaces and copies", "Locate identity constructors, project versus workspace data and copy/context ownership boundaries.", "Identifier generation combines timestamp/counter and random bytes; Project and Workspace brands have different validators. Project copies name a strategy and source/target directories. Workspace/worktree notifications describe readiness/failure or connectivity without performing boots/copies.", "Global uniqueness under every concurrency pattern, path isolation, worktree creation/removal and live workspace behavior need the implementation and relevant execution evidence."),
 ("schema.files-vcs", "Filesystem, VCS, references and pull requests", "Identify path-bearing inputs and host-owned repository answers without treating branded paths or DTOs as access control.", "Filesystem entries/matches and file events carry relative-path data. VCS describes branch, diff, status/apply and activity data. References distinguish local and Git sources. PullRequest attributes GitHub/GitLab operations to host CLI and declares typed error kinds; these schemas do not issue Git or remote commands.", "Path containment, file IO, Git behavior, remote credentials and PR publication remain implementation/runtime obligations for any claim relying on them."),
 ("schema.terminal", "PTY process and ticket DTOs", "Separate ticket representation from mint/consume authorization and process lifecycle.", "PTY records expose command/args/cwd/status/pid, lifecycle events and create/update inputs; ticket response exposes a token and positive expiry. The resize comment attributes clamping to the server, not the schema alone.", "Ticket binding/consumption, subprocess control, resize clamping and backpressure require the existing server-edge/stream evidence and relevant runtime evidence for operational guarantees."),
 ("schema.provider-integration", "Providers, credentials and integration authentication", "Distinguish secret-bearing values from safe connection references and authentication attempt state.", "Provider APIs are AISDK or Native with request headers/JSON body. Credential.Value can contain OAuth access/refresh secrets or an API key. Connection.Info exposes credential reference/label or environment variable name. Integration methods and attempt states describe the sign-in exchange; catalog events are invalidations.", "Secret storage/redaction, OAuth completion/cancellation and real provider availability require the implementation. Do not claim all Schema DTOs are redacted or that an Attempt proves authentication succeeded."),
 ("schema.developer-services", "MCP, LSP and formatter contracts", "Identify local/remote MCP configuration, display projections, auth/debug and status boundaries.", "MCP config admits local commands/environment or remote URL/headers/OAuth with timeouts. MCP Entry is a reduced endpoint projection; Debug's masking statement is producer intent and its String fields do not implement redaction. LSP/formatter modules and events describe service status.", "Project trust, process startup, resource availability, OAuth and secret masking depend on service/adapter code; no connection or debug probe was run."),
 ("schema.actions", "Actions provider automation contracts", "Separate binding revisions and prepared operation identity from side-effect commands and responses that can contain secrets.", "The Actions barrel composes identity, operation, resource, command, run and workflow contracts. Operation admission stores identity/preconditions, while ExecuteInput carries mutation JSON. CommandOutput is explicitly request-owned and may contain secret material; source comments forbid putting it in an operation row. Raw provider states and partial graph information remain representable.", "Provider-side effects, atomic admission/reconciliation, redaction and request ownership must be supported by Actions/Server/Core implementations before being claimed effective; no provider call was made."),
 ("schema.capability", "Capability references, outcomes and operator management", "Identify the distinction between data identity, Core-owned authority, opaque receipts, and bounded failure data.", "Capability explicitly assigns trusted bindings to Core. Result distinguishes completed/submitted/pending/partial/unknown, and a receipt is not a full execution receipt. FailureDetail checks serialized UTF-8 JSON size at decode and encode. Management projections expose revisions/cursors/live coverage; schedule output hides host placement and setup distinguishes verified from credential-only.", "Authority enforcement, revocation, exactly-once idempotency, pagination under mutation, credential verification and scheduler effects remain implementation/runtime claims; the schema predicates alone do not prove them."),
 ("schema.atlas", "Atlas knowledge and screen/review/setup wire contracts", "Identify host-authored knowledge anchors and transport projections without granting them Genesis review authority.", "AtlasKnowledge distinguishes proposed work identity from Task authorization and rebuilds canonical payload field order. Atlas screen/review/setup declarations model empty/present results and verdict data; multiple payloads are Unknown and therefore deliberately opaque. Declared limits/health states are not observed runtime acceptance.", "Atlas CAS, semantic governance, source realization and actual mine/index/import receipts require the relevant authority and execution. These product DTOs cannot replace the frozen two-judge oracle of this task."),
 ("schema.board", "Board planning, owner commands and merge-queue facts", "Distinguish Board projects from repository projects, Maestro writes from owner actions, and tree-scoped proof from mere status labels.", "Board separates Maestro tool inputs (required reason) and owner payloads; secrets occur in input but Attachment is a label projection. Queue/Check types bind facts to trees/attempts, with pending/error outcomes. Forecast, budget and integration rules appear in annotations/DTOs and are not computed in these modules.", "Owner enforcement, credential storage, GitHub sync/merge and budget/queue state machines remain service and runtime obligations; these schemas do not demonstrate a successful CI or merge."),
 ("schema.hook-matching", "Shared hook matching implementation", "Recognize these modules as executable matching logic shared by engine and UI, not just DTO declarations.", "HookMatch dispatches path matching to HookGlob and normalizes backslashes for other fields, with caller-supplied folding. HookGlob encodes strings to UTF-8, handles leading negation and bounded nested braces, and chooses separators using the observed platform. Comments attribute Bun compatibility; no equivalence test was executed.", "Cross-runtime equivalence, adversarial complexity/resource behavior and effective hook authorization require corresponding implementation/runtime evidence. A match is not an authorization grant."),
 ("schema.maestro", "Product Maestro context, attribution and durable events", "Identify versioned plan/context/approval/review/dispatch facts and distinguish structural attribution from verified authority.", "MaestroContext binds source/actor hashes and tool-plan references. PlanRevision V3 performs a real filter: an upstream-sourced field without upstreamAttribution fails. UpstreamAttribution is versioned, strict and explicitly does not establish host-verified authorship. Maestro distinguishes public inventory from durable-only workflow/resume events and distinguishes work acceptance from host verification.", "Hash truth, actor authority, review independence, dispatch/recovery and host verification require their actual product implementations. These product events do not establish current Genesis approval or alter the review oracle."),
 ("schema.meeting", "Meeting transcripts and owner review", "Identify session-bound final-segment records, retention/consent inputs and owner consolidation/handoff contracts.", "Meeting declares final transcript segments, kept/ephemeral retention, consent and owner confirmation states. Comments attribute append idempotency, post-stop consolidation and no automatic Atlas write to the implementation. Handoff takes selected item IDs; error reasons name lifecycle refusals.", "Deduplication, ephemeral erasure, memory consistency, consent workflow and team-message effects need service/runtime evidence; no audio/transcription or handoff was performed."),
 ("schema.schedule", "Location scheduled prompt contracts", "Separate admitted prompt results from successful model work and understand legacy ID/retry intent.", "ScheduledTask accepts short nonempty legacy IDs, generates tsk_ IDs, and declares once/hourly/daily/weekly cadence. Run is started (Session ID) or failed; comments define started as prompt admission. Existing-ID creation and slot/timezone behavior are declared implementation intent.", "Persistent deduplication, clock/timezone behavior, scheduler exclusivity and turn completion remain Core/runtime obligations; the DTO is not a distributed exactly-once guarantee."),
 ("schema.lean", "Lean reduction inventory and numeric provenance", "Distinguish supported profile labels, local savings estimates and the actual persisted-record decoder.", "Coverage lists reducer versus preserve modes and maps profiles. Engine IDs retain legacy versions. Dashboard labels savings as saved-profile history and token estimates. LeanMetrics.decode validates whitelisted record shape, accepted engine/profile, owner/model, eligibility and count arithmetic, freezes results, and returns undefined on invalid values or thrown access.", "The decoder validates supplied values, not their truth or real savings. Reducer effectiveness, recorded history and UI/host behavior require the implementation and measured execution; none was measured here."),
 ("schema.rag", "RAG pipeline diagnostic DTOs", "Identify lexical retrieval outputs and refusal/status representation without equating them with grounded answer quality.", "RagStudio fixes lexical:true and embedding:false, distinguishes unread/read/failed sources and retrieval stages, and exposes revisions, chunks, question diagnostics and comparison/pass results.", "Corpus authorization, persistence, parsing, retrieval correctness and grounded-answer quality require handlers/services and execution; DTO status labels do not supply that evidence."),
 ("schema.research", "Product research evidence, budgets and ledger contracts", "Identify binding, source representation/locator and inquiry/receipt boundaries while keeping them distinct from this task's evidence transport.", "Research uses strict structures, bounded lists/text, pinned source/reference shapes, attempts and explicit completeness/coverage. Binding names execution and authority sessions. Allowance defaults preserve historical quick tier. Inquiry and research events declare ledger facts/host-produced cards; their presence is not a factual verification result.", "Source acquisition, locator resolution, budget enforcement, publication/receipt durability and semantic truth belong to Research/Core and execution. No research tool operation or product check was performed."),
 ("schema.relay", "Relay authoring, arms, exports and ledger projections", "Separate editable draft, immutable publication, workflow execution binding, structural hook export and signed ledger verification.", "Authoring preserves unknown keys and allows incomplete drafts; publication identity is explicitly not execution authority. Hook export shape does not validate graph rules or installed state. Ledger integrity is assigned to a verifier over original bytes. External.runFromLedger derives display state from decoded bodies. Run events are supervisor facts, separate from Relay arm ledgers.", "Compiler graph checks, trust, signatures, idempotent execution, lock/crash recovery and audit truth require Relay/Core/host implementations. Source comments about these rules are not execution proofs. RelaySprint Control comments call values unrefined, but the shown schema still requires string/null forms; do not infer acceptance of arbitrary non-strings."),
 ("schema.guardrail", "Guardrail engine result contracts", "Separate rule/report transport and engine acquisition failures from actual guard execution or a Genesis verdict.", "Guardrail declares gate/warn severities, rule kinds, finding clearance, reports/errors, and separate engine-start failures. The module is a wire contract over engine output.", "Which rules ran, selected merge-base, external labels and resulting gate outcomes require engine/handler/runtime evidence; no product guard was executed."),
 ("schema.elf", "Pure ELF byte inspection", "Recognize the shared parser/admission implementation and avoid implying OS loading or an exhaustive binary-safety audit.", "Elf.inspect checks ELF64 little-endian headers, program spans/mappings and needed library metadata directly from supplied bytes. requireLibc rejects a mismatch between musl/glibc expectations and parsed dependency names. No filesystem/process/module loading occurs in this module.", "Binary authenticity, executable behavior, all loader constraints and packaging/runtime compatibility need their respective producers/loaders and execution; this source inspection is not a security certification."),
 ("schema.exports-ui", "Public export surface and UI/service notifications", "Identify barrels and event payload ownership without treating notifications as performed UI actions.", "The index reexports selected shared modules; plugin/IDE/server/installation/TUI modules define notification shapes. TUI command accepts String in addition to named literals, and toast duration has a positive default of 5000. Events do not themselves install software, render UI or execute commands.", "Subscriber behavior, publication/delivery and install/command success are separate runtime facts and remain unclaimed."),
 ("sdk.tool-facade", "SDK tool facade", "Explain the one remaining SDK member's ownership without rediscovering an implementation that is not present in the file.", "The complete two-line module reexports Failure, RegistrationError and make, plus four tool types, from @orchestra/core/tool/tool. It defines no separate registration or execution implementation. The existing SDK composition body explains the tool registration interface returned by orchestra.ts.", "Core tool construction/registration/execution internals require the actual Core implementation before new behavior claims; this facade supplies ownership only.")
]

